what is a justification a justification  is a set of reasons why something like a  belief or a claim or an action is true  or reasonable or good justifications are  often conflated with explanations an  explanation is a set of reasons why an  event or a belief came to be think back  to my video on normative versus  descriptive claims a justification  attempts to make normative sense of  something a justification tries to  rationalize whether something has a  certain quality or adheres to a value my  claim is true it has the quality of true  Ness and adheres to the value of truth  because of a B and C an explanation  tries to make descriptive sense of  something an explanation tries to  describe how something came to be based  on objective facts this event happened  because of XY and Z so let's say this I  say to you why is God real justify the  existence of the Abrahamic God and you  say back to me that's just how I grew up  my parents are Methodist I always went  to church so it's what we believe this  is not a justification for the belief in  the existence of God or a justification  for the trueness of Christian and  Methodist beliefs  it's an attempted explanation of how you  came to believe what you believe an  actual attempt to justify the existence  of God might be for you to start talking  about I've seen God perform miracles the  universe can't come from nothing here's  some direct historical or archaeological  evidence for the resurrection of Jesus  etc sometimes a justification for an  event can use some of the same facts  that would be used to explain that event  but justifying and explaining are still  different because a justification is  always going to make normative appeals  while an explanation is merely  descriptive  and that is the difference defending why  something is true or good versus  describing how something happened if  you're interested in philosophy and  critical thinking you will love  brilliant which has pretty much become  my go-to for learning things online  check out brilliance new immersive  lessons on logic problem-solving  multi-level thinking identifying false  information and identifying fallacies  whether you already have a grasp on any  of these subjects or you're looking for  a fun and engaging way to become  acquainted with these topics for the  first time brilliant really is the place  to go where you can actually learn  hands-on by solving problems and puzzles  designed by expert educators and unlike  other learning sites when I'm using  brilliant I'm actually learning by  working hands-on with real-world  scenarios and problems sign up for free  by going to brilliant org slash critical  thinking I've put a link in the  description under this video and the  first 200 people who visit will get 20%  off an annual Premium Membership visit  brilliant org slash critical thinking
 

